      "description": "Salamanca Infrastructure LLC is the U.S. midstream infrastructure owner of the Salamanca floating production system and associated oil and natural-gas export laterals at Keathley Canyon Block 689 in the deepwater U.S. Gulf of Mexico. The refurbished semi-submersible receives production from the separate Leon and Castile upstream fields and can process 60,000 barrels of oil per day and 40 million cubic feet of natural gas per day. LLOG operates the facility but is not treated as a manager-level owner. ArcLight Energy Partners Fund VII-backed affiliates financed the development through an ownership arrangement and hold a plurality ownership interest; the exact ArcLight percentage and legal investment vehicle are not publicly disclosed. Repsol completed a combined 20% sale to ArcLight and Centaurus in December 2023 and reported a retained 2.5% direct interest at year-end 2025. Public sources do not disclose a complete current capitalization table. The Leon and Castile fields, wells and leases and the subordinate Salamanca Infrastructure Finance, Salamanca FPS Infra and Salamanca OGL Infra entities are not separate PortCos. No ArcLight exit or signed pending Salamanca sale was identified through August 15, 2026.",
